    heroSubhead: "An annual physical is important for health maintenance and disease prevention. At Body1MD, your physical is led by Dr. Andrew Hemmen, a board-certified internal medicine physician, in a visit designed to last up to an hour.",
    heroImage: {"src":"/images/dr-hemmen-white-coat.jpg","alt":"Dr. Andrew Hemmen in his white coat at Body1MD in Los Ranchos de Albuquerque"},
    introHeading: "Why an Annual Physical Matters",
    intro: ["An annual physical is important for health maintenance and disease prevention. Adults who get annual physicals are more likely to discover potential health complications before they become serious, and they are more aware of the importance of lifestyle choices and how they affect overall wellbeing. Several tests and screenings are performed to verify the health of the body's various organs and systems. If a problem is uncovered during a routine check-up, treatment can begin immediately to slow or even halt its progression.","At Body1MD, a physical is not a box to check. We begin with a comprehensive consultation, looking at your health from head to toe, so we can fully understand you, your history, and your goals. From there, we make sure your core primary care needs are up to date, including preventive screenings, lipid management, and blood pressure control."],
    signsHeading: "What Your Physical May Include",
    signsList: ["A review of your personal and family health history, medications and supplements","Vital signs, including weight and blood pressure","A head-to-toe physical examination","Time to discuss any symptoms, concerns or questions you bring","Screening recommendations appropriate for your age, sex and risk factors","Laboratory testing when indicated, such as cholesterol and blood sugar","A review of your vaccinations","Lifestyle recommendations for exercise, nutrition, sleep and stress"],
